{
  "_comment": "Canonical show config consumed by scripts/build_pages.py --all. Every show entry has two roles, both fully materialised: (1) a top-level 'default' object holding the factory default parameters the runtime uses when the show is requested without explicit params (equivalently, the values the C++ ShowFactory '|' fallback in src/show/factory/ShowFactory.cpp produces for '{}'); (2) a 'variants' array of curated presets. The default is structurally distinct from variants — it is not a named entry inside the array. Every 'params' object (in 'default' and in every variant) carries every key the C++ factory reads for that show; the empty-object shorthand 'params: {}' is reserved for shows that genuinely take no parameters (ColorRun, Jump). The optional show-level 'iterations' field and the optional per-entry 'iterations' override apply to render-row count for the gallery only — they are not consumed by the firmware. Adding a new show here previews it in the gallery without any source-code change.",
